.TH C 1 "2026-09-23" "0.9.0" "cli-assistant"
.SH NAME
c \- Command Line Assistant client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Command Line Assistant client sends questions to the cli-assistant daemon
over the system D-Bus and renders the response in the terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plain
Disable colors and rich rendering.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B chat
Ask a question. If no subcommand is supplied, \fBchat\fR is used by default.
Supports stdin, attachments, interactive mode, chat management, and
\fB\-\-with-output\fR terminal context. The interactive and TUI modes carry the
recent turns as conversation context and compact older history into a summary
as it grows. Use \fBchat \-\-tui\fR for a full-screen TUI conversation window.
.TP
.B history
Read, filter, or clear conversation history.
.TP
.B feedback
Show feedback instructions.
.TP
.B shell
Install or remove shell integrations and start terminal capture.
.TP
.B setup
Run the first-time configuration wizard: prompts for the API endpoint, API key,
model (selectable from the endpoint's /models list), and reply language, writes
/etc/cli-assistant/config.toml, then restarts clad. Requires root
(\fBsudo c setup\fR). Re-running it keeps every field it does not ask about.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc.d/cla-interactive.bashrc
Bash keybinding for interactive mode.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/command-line-assistant/terminal.log
Terminal capture log while capture is active.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clad (8)
